{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b8827b9b-fd47-4b6c-8cde-7bf1cf0cc91d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae19190966d8f662","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-wm0i13tu/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E002.md","content":"# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing\nfrom the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server\ntopology. The strategy flags this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer affects\nthe HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to\ndelegate artifact operations. The outcome gates the operator implementation scope.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Determine the routing mechanism for directing artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment\n  to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (e.g. gateway-level HTTPRoute routing versus a\n  tracking-server-side delegation configuration), consistent with the operator's existing\n  conditional Gateway API pattern based on runtime CRD discovery.\n- Determine explicitly whether the MLflow tracking server needs a configuration change to\n  delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance, or whether routing can be handled\n  entirely at the ingress/gateway layer. If a server-side change is required, record the resulting\n  scope impact so it can be tracked against the server-side workspace-aware artifacts-only work.\n- Define the HTTPRoute design for the artifacts-only instance's own ingress (own Service and\n  HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking deployment's).\n- Produce a documented routing design decision sufficient to scope the operator implementation:\n  which resources are created, how the main tracking deployment is configured, and what\n  validation applies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented routing design decision covers how artifact traffic flows from the main tracking\n  deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, at a functional level without prescribing\n  implementation details beyond what the strategy states.\n- The design explicitly states whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to\n  delegate artifact operations, with the scope impact recorded if so.\n- The HTTPRoute design is consistent with the operator's existing pattern of conditional Gateway\n  API resource creation via runtime CRD discovery.\n- The downstream operator implementation scope for the split-server topology is explicitly\n  confirmed or revised based on the outcome.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nThis investigation de-risks (does not itself cover) the following strategy HLRs:\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): dedicated artifacts-only Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute — the HTTPRoute design is an\n  outcome of this investigation.\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated instance — the\n  routing mechanism is the subject of this investigation.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Misconfiguration of the split topology could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation\n  (strategy risk); the routing design must account for the operator validation that rejects\n  configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65825,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4f627a192accfe8","agent_id":"aa1207370f11fae22","session_id":"d88b54d0-1f1c-4737-bb2c-840a712cae3c","uuid":"da3f068b-e385-4694-bb33-19fca6c53cce","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:53:21.164Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
