e the plugin's existing behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact operations (no\n  regression in the fully-initialized server context).\n- Keep the authentication setup unchanged: the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name\n  kubernetes-auth` configuration work identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only\n  instance (Staff Engineer Input). Per the same input, the plugin's internal Kubernetes API\n  mechanics are implementation details of this component, not strategy-level prescriptions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The plugin resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping from artifact request context in a server\n  where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized — demonstrated through the\n  artifacts-only server serving and denying artifacts per workspace membership.\n- Workspace resolution initialization succeeds with only the workspace provider initialized (no\n  tracking store or model registry store required).\n- If refactoring was required: workspace resolution has an independent initialization path, and the\n  refactoring is documented; the plugin's `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point registration and\n  `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` loading continue to work for the tracking server unchanged.\n- Existing tracking-server workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (regression coverage for\n  non-artifact operations).\n- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup require no changes for the\n  artifacts-only context.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context\n  without tracking store initialization.\n- HLR-2 (P0, enabling): artifact-request workspace validation in the server delegates to this\n  plugin's resolution — this epic is the P0-enabling dependency for that validation path, hence its\n  P0 priority by inheritance.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The strategy's risk table flags the possible coupling of workspace resolution to the full\n  tracking server initialization path; the feasibility investigation gates this epic's scope\n  (verification-only vs. refactor).\n- The plugin is consumed by the MLflow image build as an external package; version coordination\n  with the server-side work is a planning concern, not a DAG dependency on any other epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67574,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4f627a192accfe8","agent_id":"aa1207370f11fae22","session_id":"d88b54d0-1f1c-4737-bb2c-840a712cae3c","uuid":"5c004b5f-f456-4733-9743-43470c7ceeaf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:53:54.413Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
