{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7cbfb8da4534e7e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing\n30\tfrom the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server\n31\ttopology. The strategy flags this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer affects\n32\tthe HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to\n33\tdelegate artifact operations. The outcome gates the operator implementation scope.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Determine the routing mechanism for directing artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment\n38\t  to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (e.g. gateway-level HTTPRoute routing versus a\n39\t  tracking-server-side delegation configuration), consistent with the operator's existing\n40\t  conditional Gateway API pattern based on runtime CRD discovery.\n41\t- Determine explicitly whether the MLflow tracking server needs a configuration change to\n42\t  delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance, or whether routing can be handled\n43\t  entirely at the ingress/gateway layer. If a server-side change is required, record the resulting\n44\t  scope impact so it can be tracked against the server-side workspace-aware artifacts-only work.\n45\t- Define the HTTPRoute design for the artifacts-only instance's own ingress (own Service and\n46\t  HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking deployment's).\n47\t- Produce a documented routing design decision sufficient to scope the operator implementation:\n48\t  which resources are created, how the main tracking deployment is configured, and what\n49\t  validation applies.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A documented routing design decision covers how artifact traffic flows from the main tracking\n54\t  deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, at a functional level without prescribing\n55\t  implementation details beyond what the strategy states.\n56\t- The design explicitly states whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to\n57\t  delegate artifact operations, with the scope impact recorded if so.\n58\t- The HTTPRoute design is consistent with the operator's existing pattern of conditional Gateway\n59\t  API resource creation via runtime CRD discovery.\n60\t- The downstream operator implementation scope for the split-server topology is explicitly\n61\t  confirmed or revised based on the outcome.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\tThis investigation de-risks (does not itself cover) the following strategy HLRs:\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-5 (P1): dedicated artifacts-only Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute — the HTTPRoute design is an\n68\t  outcome of this investigation.\n69\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated instance — the\n70\t  routing mechanism is the subject of this investigation.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Misconfiguration of the split topology could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation\n75\t  (strategy risk); the routing design must account for the operator validation that rejects\n76\t  configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b501ae0fcb081eb3","agent_id":"a074eb91bfb665497","session_id":"d88b54d0-1f1c-4737-bb2c-840a712cae3c","uuid":"1039ec09-77d4-4015-9b20-27a520a1bdba","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:56:37.430Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7cbfb8da4534e7e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
