rect handling given\n65\t`.context/rhai-components.txt` has no separate entries. The three implementation epics are\n66\tdistinct logical changes in distinct codebases (server, plugin, operator), not an artificial\n67\tsplit of one surface. No scope duplication: E003 enforces validation by delegating to the\n68\tplugin (with an explicit AC that the plugin capability is not reimplemented in the server),\n69\tE004 delivers the resolution, E005 deploys the topology. The E005 size overage (2-3 sprints\n70\tper the strategy's own estimate) is kept as one logical change WITH a concrete recorded\n71\tre-split trigger in the summary's Health Warnings — a managed trade-off that counts as\n72\twithin the guideline. No work-product type mixing.\n73\t\n74\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n75\tBoth Investigations genuinely resolve uncertainty that changes downstream structure:\n76\tE001's outcome determines verification-vs-refactor scope for E004 and the validation\n77\tapproach for E003; E002's outcome determines E005's routing mechanism — both carry\n78\t`gate_failure_impact` with `action: rewrite` and concrete `fallback_approach` values. All\n79\tthree gated epics have `gated_by` set, and every `gated_by` target appears in that epic's\n80\tdirect `dependencies` list. Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (server\n81\tcapability, plugin resolution path, rendered Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute topology). No\n82\tmisclassifications: neither investigation is an implementation in disguise, since each\n83\toutcome rewrites downstream scope rather than merely producing a document.\n84\t\n85\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n86\tSignal rubrics match epic types: E001/E002 carry `investigation_signals` with\n87\t`ai_signals: null`; E003/E004/E005 carry `ai_signals` with `investigation_signals: null`.\n88\tRationales in the ai-signals files match the frontmatter values and are well grounded.\n89\t`architecture_claims` calibration was checked against `.context`: E003 and E004 cite\n90\tmlflow.md (flag set, plugin version/entry-point, workspace store backing) and E005 cites\n91\tmlflow-operator.md (Helm-in-operator pattern, conditional CRD discovery) — all corroborated.\n92\tOne minor observation (see issues): E001's `source_accessibility: 1` rationale asserts the\n93\tplugin's initialization path \"can be traced\" although no architecture-context file\n94\tcorroborates the plugin's repository (E004 scores `repo_access: 0` for exactly that\n95\treason). The value remains defensible — the rubric asks whether the answer is\n96\tsource-derived rather than a pending human decision, and the plugin is a team-owned\n97\tinternal component per the strategy — so this is a rationale-precision nit, not a scoring\n98\terror. No arithmetic or threshold checks performed (computed by the pipeline).\n99\t\n100\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n101\tEvery epic has testable ACs directly derived from the strategy's acceptance criteria\n102\t(strategy ACs 1-4 appear in E003, ACs 5-6 in E005, plus plugin-specific ACs in E004).\n103\tRule-mandated ACs: no konflux-chain, docs-authoring, or replacement epic exists, and the\n104\tanalogous mandates are covered anyway — backwards-compatibility/regression ACs on E003 and\n105\tE005, operator validation rejecting misconfiguration on E005, and the end-to-end\n106\tworkspace-enforcement AC on E005 (the Rule-25-style AC gate replacing a DAG edge). No\n107\tsoft-ACs: the latency AC on E003 conditions the epic's own deliverable (measure, report,\n108\trecord the caching decision), not an externally-granted precondition; the end-to-end AC on\n109\tE005 conditions what that epic's topology verifies. No epic body references sibling epics\n110\tby draft ID — investigations are referenced by name.\n111\t\n112\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n113\tAll strategy scope is covered: flag composition, workspace validation with 403 denial,\n114\tfail-closed 503 behavior, backwards compatibility, operator split topology with traffic\n115\trouting, plugin resolution in the artifacts-only context, and P2 audit logging. All five\n116\t\"needs validation\" assumptions are carried forward (flag composability and path resolution\n117\tinto E001/E003; workspace-store accessibility into E001; single-tenant regression into\n118\tE003; chart extension into E005's scope). All four open questions are dispositioned rather\n119\tthan dropped: routing (E002), plugin coupling (E001), latency/caching (E003 measurement AC\n120\tplus a Health Warning), audit channel (Health Warning plus E003 scope note). The\n121\tintegration-testing effort is explicitly distributed as per-epic ACs with rationale in the\n122\tHealth Warnings. Staff Engineer overrides are correctly applied (no new flag, split\n123\tdeployment not a toggle, no SSAR prescription). Documentation Support is \"Pending human\n124\treview\", not \"Yes\", so Rule 11 requires no docs-authoring epic — confirmed by the validator.\n125\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb6e1148f39adc1e","agent_id":"ab7d1d56ba6718238","session_id":"d88b54d0-1f1c-4737-bb2c-840a712cae3c","uuid":"86269395-86ea-4a44-81ca-2f8dc2b2f670","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:00:44.848Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae010b93f911be30","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
