{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7e310dfc75e5d9e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Artifacts-only workspace resolution in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the plugin's workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking\n15\t    server initialization path, this epic's scope expands from verification to refactoring\n16\t    workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin,\n17\t    per the investigation's refactoring plan.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic verifies and, where needed, extends the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so that\n40\tworkspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping via the workspace store, registered through\n41\tthe `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) functions\n42\tcorrectly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are\n43\tnot initialized. Today the plugin provides workspace-scoped authorization for the tracking\n44\tserver's non-artifact operations; the artifacts-only proxy needs to call the same workspace\n45\tresolution logic before proxying artifact requests to the storage backend. Whether this is\n46\tverification-only or requires refactoring depends on the outcome of the workspace resolution\n47\tfeasibility investigation: if workspace resolution is currently coupled to the full tracking\n48\tserver initialization path, it must be factored into an independent initialization path within the\n49\tplugin.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Verify that the plugin's workspace resolution initializes and resolves experiment-to-workspace\n54\t  mapping in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized,\n55\t  exercising it from the artifacts-only server's artifact request path.\n56\t- If the feasibility investigation finds coupling to the full tracking server initialization path:\n57\t  refactor workspace resolution within the plugin into an independent initialization path, so the\n58\t  artifacts-only server can initialize only the workspace provider.\n59\t- Preserve the plugin's existing behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact operations (no\n60\t  regression in the fully-initialized server context).\n61\t- Keep the authentication setup unchanged: the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name\n62\t  kubernetes-auth` configuration work identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only\n63\t  instance (Staff Engineer Input). Per the same input, the plugin's internal Kubernetes API\n64\t  mechanics are implementation details of this component, not strategy-level prescriptions.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- The plugin resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping from artifact request context in a server\n69\t  where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized — demonstrated through the\n70\t  artifacts-only server serving and denying artifacts per workspace membership.\n71\t- Workspace resolution initialization succeeds with only the workspace provider initialized (no\n72\t  tracking store or model registry store required).\n73\t- If refactoring was required: workspace resolution has an independent initialization path, and the\n74\t  refactoring is documented; the plugin's `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point registration and\n75\t  `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` loading continue to work for the tracking server unchanged.\n76\t- Existing tracking-server workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (regression coverage for\n77\t  non-artifact operations).\n78\t- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup require no changes for the\n79\t  artifacts-only context.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context\n84\t  without tracking store initialization.\n85\t- HLR-2 (P0, enabling): artifact-request workspace validation in the server delegates to this\n86\t  plugin's resolution — this epic is the P0-enabling dependency for that validation path, hence its\n87\t  P0 priority by inheritance.\n88\t\n89\t## Risks / Notes\n90\t\n91\t- The strategy's risk table flags the possible coupling of workspace resolution to the full\n92\t  tracking server initialization path; the feasibility investigation gates this epic's scope\n93\t  (verification-only vs. refactor).\n94\t- The plugin is consumed by the MLflow image build as an external package; version coordination\n95\t  with the server-side work is a planning concern, not a DAG dependency on any other epic.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81a12a139591797f","agent_id":"a7b1941eebde0cb91","session_id":"d88b54d0-1f1c-4737-bb2c-840a712cae3c","uuid":"8f0e56e2-3990-4b84-a477-0ad6b9c60b34","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:03:09.433Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7e310dfc75e5d9e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
