{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3597af473549d49","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Split-server artifact serving topology in the MLflow operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design requires a tracking-server-side delegation\n15\t    configuration rather than gateway-level HTTPRoute routing, the operator's artifact\n16\t    traffic routing and main tracking deployment configuration are redesigned accordingly,\n17\t    and any required server-side change is recorded as follow-up scope against the\n18\t    server-side workspace-aware artifacts-only work.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Split-server artifact serving topology in the MLflow operator\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the split-server topology in the MLflow operator: a dedicated artifacts-only\n41\tMLflow instance deployed as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, plus the\n42\tconfiguration of the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated\n43\tinstance. The main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and\n44\tprompt registry, while the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace\n45\tvalidation. This is a topology change in the operator, not a single-deployment configuration flag\n46\t(Staff Engineer / SME Input). The operator uses its existing Helm-in-operator pattern — the MLflow\n47\tCR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, and applied via\n48\tServer-Side Apply — so the split deployment is delivered as new chart templates plus updates to\n49\tthe main tracking Deployment's configuration.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only instance: dedicated Deployment, Service, and\n54\t  HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n55\t- Updates to the main tracking Deployment's rendered configuration to route artifact traffic to\n56\t  the dedicated artifacts-only instance, following the routing mechanism determined by the\n57\t  artifact traffic routing design investigation (gateway-level HTTPRoute routing versus a\n58\t  tracking-server-side delegation configuration).\n59\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n60\t  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n61\t  mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment, together with\n62\t  `--artifacts-only` and `--serve-artifacts`.\n63\t- HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the\n64\t  operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies (Gateway API).\n65\t- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main\n66\t  tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n67\t- Operator validation that rejects configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks the\n68\t  workspace flags when workspace-aware artifact serving is intended (strategy risk mitigation\n69\t  against artifact requests bypassing workspace validation through misconfiguration).\n70\t- Users configure a single MLflow CR; the operator manages the split topology declaratively.\n71\t- End-to-end integration verification of the split topology: artifact requests through the\n72\t  operator-deployed topology are served for workspace members and denied for non-members once the\n73\t  server-side workspace-aware artifacts-only capability is available (this is an acceptance gate on\n74\t  this epic's deliverable, not a dependency on the server work — chart and reconciler development\n75\t  proceeds in parallel).\n76\t\n77\t## Acceptance Criteria\n78\t\n79\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator reconciles the\n80\t  CR, then the operator creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute\n81\t  separate from the main tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment\n82\t  resources with the correct flag combinations.\n83\t- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, the artifacts-only\n84\t  Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://\n85\t  --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the container command in\n86\t  the rendered Deployment spec.\n87\t- The main tracking deployment's rendered configuration routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n88\t  artifacts-only instance per the routing design (verified by the rendered resources and\n89\t  configuration).\n90\t- The operator rejects invalid configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks the\n91\t  workspace flags required for workspace-aware artifact serving, with a clear validation error.\n92\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created only when the Gateway API CRDs\n93\t  are present at runtime (conditional discovery behavior verified both with and without the CRDs).\n94\t- End-to-end through the operator-deployed split topology: an artifact request from a workspace\n95\t  member is served (HTTP 200) and a request from a non-member is denied (HTTP 403), verified\n96\t  against the workspace-aware artifacts-only server capability.\n97\t- Deployments that do not enable the split-server artifact serving retain the current single\n98\t  deployment topology unchanged (backwards compatibility regression).\n99\t\n100\t## HLR Traceability\n101\t\n102\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with\n103\t  its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n104\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only\n105\t  instance.\n106\t\n107\t## Risks / Notes\n108\t\n109\t- Split-deployment operational complexity (strategy risk): two Deployments, two Services, two\n110\t  HTTPRoutes, and artifact traffic routing configuration increase the operational surface; the\n111\t  operator manages the topology declaratively from a single MLflow CR, and operator validation\n112\t  guards against misconfiguration that could bypass workspace validation.\n113\t- The routing mechanism depends on the routing design investigation's outcome; if the outcome\n114\t  requires a tracking-server-side delegation configuration instead of gateway-level routing, this\n115\t  epic's routing scope is rewritten accordingly.\n116\t- Effort estimate for this scope is 2-3 sprints per the strategy; see the decomposition summary's\n117\t  health warnings for the recorded re-split trigger.\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81a12a139591797f","agent_id":"a7b1941eebde0cb91","session_id":"d88b54d0-1f1c-4737-bb2c-840a712cae3c","uuid":"c43b8020-8b26-43b6-9bd8-986340958048","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:03:10.711Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3597af473549d49","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
